[00:06.56]1. Ev’ry newborn child, Ev’ry drop of rain,
[00:14.98]Ev’ry golden ray of sun, Each head of grain—
[00:22.24]All are gifts from God; They reveal his way.
[00:29.54]Miracles performed by him sustain us each day.
[00:36.28](Chorus)
[00:36.28]So, what are we to do with a gift so rare
[00:42.92]But to love the One who gave it and show him we care.
[00:50.74]No matter what we do, We never can earn it.
[00:57.16]This gift is still a gift—The miracle of life.
[01:12.78]2. Others may give up, Lose their will to try,
[01:20.02]Echoing the wife of Job: “Curse God and die.”
[01:26.98]We are not that way; Praise to God we give,
[01:34.12]Thanking him for ev’ry precious moment we live.
[01:41.06](Chorus)
[01:41.06]So, what are we to do with a gift so rare
[01:47.78]But to love the ones around us and show them we care.
[01:55.56]No matter what we do, We never can earn it.
[02:02.02]This gift is still a gift—The miracle of life.
